From: postmarketOS mojito port
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: let the invoke wait be frozen across suspend

The reverse-tunnel server (hexagonrpcd) is normally blocked in an invoke, waiting
for the DSP. Freezing it for suspend interrupts the wait, the ioctl returns
-ERESTARTSYS and is restarted, which sends the invoke to the DSP again while the
first is outstanding. On the Redmi Note 10 the ADSP crashed right after every
resume. Sleep in a freezable state so the freezer does not interrupt the task.
---
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c	2026-11-27 08:23:03.746770098 +0500
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c	2026-11-27 08:23:03.764231255 +0500
@@ -1328,7 +1328,12 @@
 		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ctx->work, 10 * HZ))
 			err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else {
-		err = wait_for_completion_interruptible(&ctx->work);
+		/*
+		 * Freezable: a DSP listener sleeps here across system suspend. An interrupted
+		 * invoke is restarted, which sends the same message to the DSP a second time.
+		 */
+		err = wait_for_completion_state(&ctx->work,
+						TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE);
 	}
 
 	return err;
